# =============================================================================
# Patient data and derived per-patient files.
#
# The rule: nothing with one row per patient gets committed. The source clinical
# CSV, the derived label/cohort/manifest tables, and the saved prediction and
# embedding arrays all carry a de-identified patient identifier joined to an
# outcome (ICU / ventilation / death). Aggregate outputs -- per-fold metrics,
# column-level specifications, fitted summary statistics -- are safe and are
# committed so results are readable without rerunning anything.
#
# Everything ignored here regenerates by running the pipeline in the order
# documented in README.md.
# =============================================================================

# --- imaging archive (2.1 GB, 13,638 files; redownload from Kaggle) ----------
COVID-19-NY-SBU/
covid-19-cxr-ny-sbu.zip
*.kaggle-partial

# --- source clinical data (1384 patient rows with outcomes) ------------------
deidentified_overlap_tcia.csv*
patient_details.csv
metadata.csv
MIDRC-RICORD-*.xlsx
midrc-ricord-*.zip

# --- derived per-patient tables ----------------------------------------------
visor_labels.csv
visor_cohort.csv
visor_manifest.csv
visor_manifest_split.csv

# --- saved arrays: all of these are one row per patient ----------------------
# resnet50_embeddings*.npz hold p_* (patient IDs) and y_* (labels) alongside the
# 2048-d features. test_preds_*.npz hold y_true plus per-patient predictions in
# split order, which reconstructs the test outcome vector. Both are row-level
# patient outcome data despite looking like intermediate model artifacts.
*.npz

# --- credentials --------------------------------------------------------------
kaggle.json
.kaggle/

# --- editor / tool config (not part of methods or results) --------------------
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately COMMITTED (listed for the next reader, not as ignore rules):
#
#   *.py                              all pipeline scripts
#   README.md                         pipeline order, results, limitations
#   feature_spec.csv                  column-level leakage audit, no patient rows
#   norm_stats.json                   aggregate pixel mean/std
#   impute_stats.json                 aggregate train medians/modes
#   final_test_results.csv            5 rows, model-level metrics
#   multiseed_ablations.csv           6 rows, seed-level metrics
#   finetune_multiseed.csv            15 rows, fold-level metrics
#   ablation_*.csv, fusion_cv_*.csv   5 rows each, fold-level metrics
#   calibration_fusion_results.csv    2 rows, model-level metrics
#   *.png                             calibration plots, aggregate only
#
# No model weight files exist -- nothing is checkpointed to disk. Every model is
# trained inside the run that evaluates it, so weights would need saving
# deliberately if you ever want them committed.
# =============================================================================
